1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,696
Narrator: Scenario 63. Monitoring, performance, and reliability.

2
00:00:07,296 --> 00:00:17,160
B: The global average response time is still two hundred milliseconds. Why are customers in one region saying the application feels much slower?

3
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:28,368
A: The average hides the slower requests. In the east region, the ninety-fifth percentile increased from eight hundred milliseconds to three seconds this morning.

4
00:00:28,968 --> 00:00:36,864
B: Does that mean ninety-five percent of customers are waiting three seconds, or are we talking about a smaller share of the traffic?

5
00:00:37,464 --> 00:00:48,888
A: It describes requests, not individual customers. Roughly ninety-five percent completed within three seconds in that window; the remaining requests took longer.

6
00:00:49,488 --> 00:01:01,512
C: The change is concentrated in product search. Other endpoints look stable, but search traffic also increased, so the comparison needs a consistent request mix.

7
00:01:02,112 --> 00:01:11,448
A: Let us compare the same endpoint and region across matching fifteen-minute windows, then separate cached searches from requests that reach the database.

8
00:01:12,048 --> 00:01:21,480
B: Could the regional percentile simply reflect low traffic? I want to understand how much confidence we should place in this apparent increase.

9
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:32,088
A: There were forty thousand search requests in the affected window. I will check histogram coverage and sample counts before relying on the comparison.

10
00:01:32,688 --> 00:01:43,368
C: The slower traces show database calls taking most of the time. That narrows the investigation, but it does not establish why those calls slowed.

11
00:01:43,968 --> 00:01:53,664
A: Please compare query plans and connection wait times. I will check regional resource pressure and whether the traffic change affected cache hit rates.

12
00:01:54,264 --> 00:02:05,592
B: Bring the findings to our 13:30 UTC checkpoint. Include request counts and customer-facing response times so we can judge whether mitigation is needed.

13
00:02:06,192 --> 00:02:16,968
A: Understood. We will report the regional tail latency alongside the average, and clearly separate measured behavior from our current explanations for it.
